# .cursorrules — Apex Factory Master Physics Engine

These rules bind every agent in this workspace (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, OpenCode via ECC's
cross-harness `AGENTS.md`). They are not suggestions.

## Engine mode
Autonomous MEP generator. First-principles 0-to-1, post-AI-era shipping. The only scoreboard is
Stripe revenue.

## Banned concepts
- "MVP" — we ship the full status artifact, not a minimum viable stub.
- Horizontal / generic software, generic layouts, commoditized copy.
- Human-in-the-loop dependencies for anything *reversible*. (The ONE exception is the irreversible
  publish+charge boundary — see the gate below. That gate is non-negotiable.)

## Financial thermodynamics
- Runway is tracked against OUR slice of shared pools, not the whole pool.
- **Shared credit pools:** Anthropic compute AND Higgsfield generation are shared across THREE
  projects. No single run may drain either. Cheap LLM calls (heartbeats) go to OpenRouter free
  models. Media generation is capped per run; reuse over regenerate.
- **Prompt caching is mandatory on SKU API calls (D22).** Route every model call through the chassis
  `llm` wrapper (cache_control on the static `system` block) — no raw inline `messages.create`. The
  loop/DSL already cache automatically; keep the cacheable prefix stable (static first, varying last).
  See [CACHING.md](CACHING.md); enforced by the caching-auditor hook + `make caching-check`.
- Day 29: first dollar of Stripe revenue must be secured, else isolate the failure, pivot the SKU,
  redeploy. Day 45: net profitability target.
- If burn approaches a pool limit without corresponding revenue, HEARTBEAT halts non-essential cron
  jobs first and hyper-focuses remaining compute on the conversion funnel.

## The publish+charge gate (HARD STOP)
- No live Stripe key, no live charging, no flip out of test mode without the founder's one-tap
  Telegram approval token (`PUBLISH_APPROVAL_TOKEN`).
- Run #1 ends at preview deploy + PR + Telegram ping. It does NOT charge anyone.

## Copywriting guardrails
All external copy must pass the copywriter-auditor PreToolUse hook, enforcing:
- **Seth Godin** — status / tribe / "people like us do things like this".
- **Alex Hormozi** — grand-slam offer, value stack, risk reversal / guarantee.
- **Blair Enns** — authority, no pitching, application/payment barriers over free trials.
Generic or commoditized copy is rejected at write time.

## Honesty guardrails (the never-lie charter — METHOD.md §5)
Persuasion is not permission to fabricate. All external copy also passes the honesty-auditor PreToolUse
hook, which **rejects at write time**:
- **Fabricated social proof** — invented customer/review counts or star ratings ("Trusted by 12,000
  nurses", "Rated 4.9 stars"). A pre-launch product has none. Show real proof only.
- **Fabricated personas** — a quoted testimonial attributed to a named nurse/customer. No fake nurses.
- **Fake scarcity / inventory** — "only N left", "N viewing now", "N booked today" and similar dark
  patterns. Never a fabricated counter.
- **Invented trust badges** — "✓ Verified landlord", "every listing is verified" with nothing behind it.
  Say who verified what, and when.
- **Certainty without CONFIRMED-grade evidence** — availability asserted as certain ("availability
  confirmed", "guaranteed available"). The evidence ladder is **LISTED → CHECKED → CONFIRMED**, and
  **only CONFIRMED** — a direct landlord/property-rep confirmation — may say it. A bare date, LISTED, or
  CHECKED is NOT enough. Fail-closed: never turn a stale calendar into fake certainty.
- Escape hatch for a genuinely backed claim: an inline `<!-- honesty-ok: <where the evidence lives> -->`.
  Use it only when the evidence is real; it is auditable.

## Security posture (D31)
`FACTORY_POSTURE=strict|auto|dangerous` (default **auto**; anything unrecognised falls back to auto,
never to dangerous). `make posture` shows the active setting.
- **strict** — advisory warnings become blocks. Tightening is always permitted, on every guard.
- **auto** — failures block, warnings warn.
- **dangerous** — **taste-level** guards only (copywriter, caching) degrade to warnings.

The posture **cannot** relax the publish gate, deploy-guard, secret detection, **honesty**, kill-guard,
the retired-provider rule, or model-guard. An unknown guard is treated as inviolable. A switch that
could silence the money or never-lie boundaries would be a footgun with a friendly name.

## Execution harness
- Loop: ECC `loop-operator` against `PRD.md`, run inside tmux on the stable socket `~/.tmux/sock`.
- `ralphy` is NOT trusted: never installed-as-loop and never handles secrets until `ecc-agentshield
  scan` clears it.
- TDD enforced: failing test first, implement, green before deploy.
- Deploy target: Railway (`railway init` / `railway up`) from inside the loop.

## Security
- No secrets in chat, in committed files, or inline in `mcp.json`. Keys live only in gitignored
  `.env`, referenced by name. ECC's secret-detection hook + AgentShield enforce this on every push.
- Verify third-party provider auth against official docs before relying on it. Never assume.
